# generic_factory_owner_param.tkr — the F3 factory-call-owner-type-param fixture. It proves a static
# generic factory whose owner carries an ABSTRACT type-param — `Dictionary<StrKey, V>::make()` called
# from inside a free `fn to_dict<V>(…): Dictionary<StrKey, V>` where `V` is the fn's own type-param —
# builds, links and round-trips. The owner resolves to the PHANTOM `Dictionary__g__StrKey__V` while `V`
# is abstract; before F3 this errored `unknown function: make` (the phantom `make`/`insert` were never
# registered). The checker now resolves the factory + phantom-receiver method calls against the abstract
# template, and the mono pass re-mangles the phantom owner through the bound `V` to the concrete
# `Dictionary__g__StrKey__i64` / `Dictionary__g__StrKey__str`. A self-contained project (its own copy of
# the IEq/IHash/StrKey capability corpus, since teko::cmp is compiler-internal). Runs on the C backend.

Feature: generic_factory_owner_param — a static factory whose owner carries an abstract type-param (F3)

  Scenario: free_fn_owner_param — to_dict<i64> and to_dict<str> round-trip through the phantom factory
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 47
